On offer
    If player is karus
        Say "Monsters have grown brave and are increasingly attacking merchants and civilian residents so we're trying to locate their hide out and wipe them out. I can only send you as a party no matter how strong you are. It's for your own good. Don't object."
        Topic "Tell me more..." do
            Show quest "I hear the monsters have taken refuge in the Delok Creek in Kartia Desert. If you kill Ripper, their leader, and bring me the proof, you don't have to worry about going. I've already pulled some strings.\n\nGet Captain Fargo's monster suppression squad request, join the squad, kill their leader Ripper and bring the captain the proof."
    If player is elmorad
        Say "Monsters have grown brave and are increasingly attacking merchants and civilian residents so we're trying to locate their hide out and wipe them out. I can only send you as a party no matter how strong you are. It's for your own good. Don't object."
        Topic "Tell me more..." do
            Show quest "I hear the monsters have taken refuge in the Delok Creek in Kartia Desert. If you kill Ripper, their leader, and bring me the proof, you don't have to worry about going. I've already pulled some strings.\n\nGet Captain Falkwine's monster suppression squad request, join the squad, kill their leader Ripper and bring the captain the proof."

On in_progress
    Say "You have to kill Monster Leader Ripper and bring back proof. Don't tell me you still haven't even gone near him.\n\nAre you joining the monster suppression squad?"
    Topic "[Enter Dungeon]" do
        Enter instance 82 set 1 at 204 197

On ready
    If player is karus
        Say "This is the proof. If we take this to Fargo, he will give a reward."
    If player is elmorad
        Say "This is the proof. If we take this to Falkwine, he will give a reward."

On claimable
    If player is karus
        Show quest "Great. Here's your reward. Knew you'd be able to do it."
    If player is elmorad
        Show quest "All right. Here's the reward. Knew you could do it."
